{
  "category": "Protein",
  "summary": "354 Protein items audited. The category is dominated by systematic dataset-import damage: the `name` field of most items is word-salad formed by appending the (often wrong) parent's name, e.g. id `chicken` is named \"chicken meatball\", id `crab` is named \"crab fish ball\", id `mahi-mahi` is named \"mahi\", id `tempeh` is named \"tempeh vegan burger\". Parent/child trees are badly broken: ALL crustaceans/shellfish (crab, lobster, shrimp, prawn) are parented under a generic \"fish ball\" node and imitation seafood under \"surimi\"; tofu/tempeh/seitan/TVP are all parented under \"vegan burger\"; every sausage variety is parented under \"boar\"; quail egg sits in Protein parented under \"quail\" while a duplicate already lives in Dairy & Eggs. Dietary tags are also systemically wrong: NOT ONE of ~112 fish/seafood items carries the Pescatarian tag the schema supports, and gluten-containing seitan items are tagged or treated inconsistently (the base `seitan` lacks Gluten-Free, which is correct, but `textured-vegetable-protein` is fine and tofu is fine). Coverage is simultaneously over-deep in some niches (8 oyster appellations, 7 crawfish species, many redundant cut sub-cuts) and badly under-broad on the species that actually appear in everyday recipes worldwide: NO tilapia, catfish, haddock, halibut, sea bass, snapper, grouper, sole/flounder, monkfish, branzino, barramundi, milkfish, pomfret, rohu/catla, perch/walleye/pike, hake/whiting, arctic char, smelt; NO wagyu/skirt-vs-flank clarity; NO organ meats beyond liver (no kidney, tongue, heart, tripe, sweetbreads, marrow, trotters); NO game/exotic (frog legs, escargot, alligator, kangaroo, venison is present but no rabbit/hare gaps, no guinea fowl, squab, partridge); and NO edamame/natto/yuba/tofu-skin or firm/silken/extra-firm tofu subtypes. Recommendations below: fix the mangled names + broken parent trees as cleanups, add Pescatarian to all seafood, dedupe the egg, and add ~95 globally-relevant new items.",
  "issues": [
    "MANGLED NAMES (systemic, ~150+ items): the display `name` is corrupted by an appended parent token. Examples: id `chicken` name=\"chicken meatball\" (should be \"chicken meatball\" only if it IS a meatball, but it is parented under generic `meatball` and is clearly meant to be the chicken-meatball node), id `chicken-meat` name=\"chicken\" (this is the real chicken node), id `crab` name=\"crab fish ball\", id `mahi-mahi` name=\"mahi\", id `mahi-mahi-steak` name=\"mahi steak\", id `skin-on` name=\"skin on mahi\", id `salmon-oily-fish` name=\"salmon\", id `lobster` name=\"lobster fish ball\", id `shrimp-fish-ball` name=\"shrimp fish ball\", id `octopus-whole` etc. Names should be the clean product name without the parent suffix.",
    "BROKEN PARENT TREE - shellfish: crab (`crab`), lobster (`lobster`), and shrimp (`shrimp-fish-ball`) are parented under `fish-ball` (\"fish ball\"). Crustaceans are not fish balls. Their many children (dungeness, snow-crab, king-crab, stone-crab, spanner, peekytoe) inherit the wrong tree. They should be top-level shellfish or under a 'Seafood' node, not under a processed fish-paste product.",
    "BROKEN PARENT TREE - plant proteins: tofu has no parent (ok) but tempeh, seitan, TVP and every veggie-burger variant are parented under `vegan-burger` (\"vegan burger\"). Tempeh, seitan and TVP are base ingredients, not types of burger. soybean(`soybean`) is parented under tempeh and named \"soybean tempeh vegan burger\".",
    "BROKEN PARENT TREE - sausages: id `sausage` is named \"sausage boar\" and parented under `boar`; its aliases lump chorizo/bologna/pepperoni/mortadella/polish/smoked sausage into one node. Meanwhile dedicated `chorizo`, `bratwurst`, `kielbasa`, `bologna`, `pepperoni`, `mortadella`, `italian-sausage`, `andouille` exist separately under `cured-meat`. The generic `sausage` node is mis-parented and its alias list is misleading.",
    "MISPLACED + DUPLICATE EGG: id `egg-quail` (\"egg quail\") sits in category Protein, but eggs live in Dairy & Eggs where `quail-egg` (\"quail egg\") already exists. `egg-quail` is a misplaced duplicate.",
    "NO PESCATARIAN TAG ON ANY SEAFOOD: ~112 fish/shellfish/roe/surimi items exist; zero carry the `Pescatarian` dietaryTag even though the schema supports it. Every finfish, shellfish, mollusc, cephalopod, roe/caviar and surimi item should include Pescatarian.",
    "OVER-SPECIFIC / LOW-VALUE LEAF ITEMS with mangled names that read as junk: `back` (\"back chicken meatball\"), `gizzard` (\"gizzard chicken meatball\"), `fan`/`drum`/`burger`/`steak` ostrich children, `meat` (\"meat mussel\"), `tubes`/`tentacles` calamari, `skin-on` (\"skin on mahi\"). Several look like scraped sub-options rather than real catalog ingredients.",
    "AGGREGATED ALIAS LISTS hide distinct products: `salmon-oily-fish` folds canned salmon, smoked salmon (cold & hot), fresh fillet, pink/red salmon into ONE item with a Pantry shelf-life of [365,1095] AND Refrigerated [1,2] — canned and fresh salmon are different products with different storage and should not share one node. Same pattern on `cured-meat` and `tuna` (no canned-vs-fresh split).",
    "THIN FINFISH COVERAGE: only ~13 finfish species exist (cod, tuna, salmon, trout, herring, sardine, anchovy, mackerel, swordfish, mahi-mahi, eel, carp species, pollock). 'White fish' exists only as \"white fish ball\". The everyday global fish list (tilapia, catfish, haddock, halibut, sea bass, snapper, grouper, sole, flounder, etc.) is entirely missing.",
    "ORGAN/OFFAL nearly absent: only liver (beef/chicken/lamb/pork/turkey/veal) plus oxtail and a few necks. No kidney, tongue, heart, tripe, sweetbreads, marrow bones, trotters/pig feet, blood — all common in global home cooking (e.g. menudo, dirty rice, steak-and-kidney, beef tongue tacos, marrow).",
    "SHELF-LIFE inconsistency on identical product classes: fresh finfish split between Refrigerated default (cod, swordfish, mahi) and Frozen default (tuna, herring, sardine, anchovy, trout, eel) with no obvious reason; the generic `oily-fish` defaults to Frozen.",
    "GLUTEN-FREE applied near-universally (351/354). Verify seitan-family items never carry Gluten-Free (seitan is wheat gluten). `seitan` correctly omits it, but confirm any future seitan additions do too. Also confirm breaded/processed items (imitation crab/surimi typically contains wheat starch) are not blanket-tagged Gluten-Free — `imitation-crab` etc. are currently tagged Gluten-Free which is often false for commercial surimi."
  ],
  "redundancies": [
    ["egg-quail", "quail-egg", "egg-quail (Protein) duplicates quail-egg which already exists in Dairy & Eggs; remove the Protein one"],
    ["chicken", "chicken-meatball-concept", "id `chicken` is the chicken-meatball node but its bare id `chicken` plus name collide conceptually with the real chicken node `chicken-meat`; the ids are swapped/confusing and should be renamed (chicken-meatball / chicken)"],
    ["sausage", "italian-sausage", "generic `sausage` (named 'sausage boar') overlaps the dedicated italian-sausage/bratwurst/chorizo nodes via its alias list; collapse generic into a true parent or trim aliases"],
    ["mahi-mahi", "skin-on", "`skin-on` (\"skin on mahi\") is a trivial skin-on variant of mahi-mahi, not a distinct ingredient"],
    ["mussel", "meat", "id `meat` (\"meat mussel\") and `mussel-whole` are redundant presentation variants of mussel"],
    ["calamari", "tentacles", "`tentacles`/`tubes` (calamari) and `calamari-whole` are cut/presentation variants of one squid product (also overlaps `squid`)"],
    ["squid", "calamari", "`squid` (\"squid fish ball\") and `calamari` are the same animal; one is the culinary term for the other"],
    ["octopus", "tentacle", "`tentacle` (\"octopus tentacle\") and `octopus-whole` are presentation variants of octopus"],
    ["crab", "dungeness", "tree is fine in concept (species under crab) but `crab` is mis-named/mis-parented under fish-ball; flagged for the cleanup not removal"],
    ["corned-beef", "corned-beef-brisket", "corned-beef, corned-beef-brisket and `hash` (\"hash corned beef\") heavily overlap; hash is a prepared dish not a raw ingredient"]
  ],
